</address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATABE TERUHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAI, SHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUREHA KAGAKU KOGYO KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATABE, TERUHIDE</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARAI SHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATABE TERUHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAI, SHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATABE, TERUHIDE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An antistatic resin composition which comprises a thermoplastic resin comprising a graft copolymer obtained by the graft polymerization of an ethylenic unsaturated monomer to a rubbery backbone polymer having alkylene oxide moieties obtained by an emulsion polymerization using a carboxylic acid-based surfactant, and an anionic surfactant having a starting temperature for the weight decrease by heat of 250  DEG C or higher. The antistatic resin composition can be efficiently produced commercially, and can provide moldings which have excellent permanent antistatic property and are not susceptible to clouding or discoloration even when it is processed under severe conditions.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition de résine antistatique qui comprend une résine thermoplastique à base de copolymère greffé obtenu par polymérisation par greffage d'un monomère éthylénique insaturé sur un polymère à squelette linéaire caoutchouteux comportant des fractions d'oxyde d'alkylène, lequel est obtenu par polymérisation par émulsion au moyen d'un tensioactif carboxylique à base d'acide, et d'un tensioactif anionique ayant une température de départ pour la diminution de poids par la chaleur égale ou supérieure à 250 DEG  C. La composition considérée peut être produite commercialement de manière efficace, et elle permet de réaliser des moulages qui présentent d'excellentes propriétés antistatiques permanentes, sans être sensibles à l'ombrage ou à la décoloration même s'ils sont traités dans des conditions sévères.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>